    q("The chairman of a local government council is", ["appointed by the governor", "elected by the people of the area", "appointed by the President", "selected by the councillors from their number"], 1, "Section 7 requires a democratically elected council, so the chairman and councillors are elected. Caretaker committees are a departure from the constitutional requirement."),
    q("Which of the following is a function of local government?", ["Maintenance of local markets and motor parks", "Issuing international passports", "Defending the country", "Conducting federal elections"], 0, "Markets and motor parks are classic local functions. Passports, defence and federal elections are federal."),
    q("The Federal Character Commission exists to", ["allocate revenue to states", "ensure that appointments reflect the diversity of the country", "conduct elections", "audit public accounts"], 1, "It polices the federal character principle in appointments. Revenue is the RMAFC's, elections INEC's, and audits the Auditor-General's."),
